          "body": "![security-high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/security-high-priority.svg) ![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nValidate that the `owner` (if provided in the request body) matches the authenticated user's identity (`authContext.userId`). Currently, any client can specify an arbitrary `owner` in the request body, allowing them to link connections to other users' accounts or perform unauthorized operations.\n\n```suggestion\nfunction assertIdentityMatches(body: Record<string, any>, authContext: RouteAuthContext): void {\n  const bodyUserId = asOptionalString(body.userId);\n  if (bodyUserId && bodyUserId !== authContext.userId) {\n    throw {\n      code: 'TENANT_ACCESS_DENIED',\n      message: 'identity mismatch',\n      status: 403,\n    };\n  }\n\n  const owner = asConnectionOwner(body.owner);\n  if (owner && owner.kind === 'user' && owner.userId !== authContext.userId) {\n    throw {\n      code: 'TENANT_ACCESS_DENIED',\n      message: 'identity mismatch',\n      status: 403,\n    };\n  }\n\n```"
