          "author": "gemini-code-assist",
          "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nCatch and handle rejections on the `previous` promise when chaining the queue tail and awaiting execution. If a previous sync request fails, its promise will reject, causing `await previous` to throw and fail all subsequent sync requests on the same connection without executing them.\n\n```typescript\n    const previous = this.syncExecutionQueue.get(connectionId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n    let releaseCurrent!: () => void;\n    const current = new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n      releaseCurrent = resolve;\n    });\n    const queueTail = previous.catch(() => {}).then(() => current);\n    this.syncExecutionQueue.set(connectionId, queueTail);\n\n    await previous.catch(() => {});\n```"
