          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Strip mount prefixes using resolved path values**\n\nWhen `toHono` is mounted on a parameterized base path (for example `app.route('/:tenant', toHono(router))`), `mountPrefix` is derived from route patterns like `/:tenant/*`, but `toMountedRequest` compares that pattern literally against the concrete URL pathname (such as `/acme/providers`). The prefix check therefore fails and the forwarded request path is not rewritten, so the Superfunctions router receives `/acme/...` instead of `/...` and mounted routes return 404 for dynamic mounts.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
