          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow canonical Flask callbacks without provider query**\n\nFor the canonical `/callback` route, OAuth providers normally return only `code` and `state`; this forwards a missing `provider` to `_handle_callback`, which then returns a provider-required validation error. Any app that registers `/api/plugfn/callback` as its redirect URI (the canonical route exposed by the adapter) cannot finish OAuth unless the provider also happens to append a nonstandard `provider` query parameter.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
