          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Claim webhook idempotency keys atomically before dispatch**\n\nWhen the provider retries the same delivery concurrently, both requests can complete the earlier receipt lookup before either reaches this creation call. `createReceipt` also implements only a lookup-then-create, and the generated database schema has a non-unique index on `(provider, idempotencyKey)`, so both requests can create deliveries and invoke the workflow handler, duplicating side effects. Atomically claim a unique provider/idempotency key and dispatch only for the request that created the claim.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
