          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Scope TypeScript custom cache keys to the connection**\n\nWhen an application supplies the same custom cache key for calls from different users, connections, providers, or actions, this uses that key verbatim rather than including the isolation fields used by `generateKey`. The later caller can consequently receive the first caller's cached provider data without executing or validating its own request; even within one tenant, reusing a key across actions can return the wrong response shape. Namespace custom keys by provider, action, user, and resolved connection before lookup.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
