      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Parse the Outlook payload before verifying clientState**\n\nFor webhook requests handled by `handleWebhookRoute`, `verifyWebhook` is called with `payload` set to `undefined` and the JSON available only in `options.rawBody`. The verifier is therefore invoked with `undefined` before `parseWebhookPayload` runs, while Outlook's verifier calls `verifyOutlookClientState(payload, secret)` and necessarily returns false. With the default signature-verification behavior, every valid Outlook notification is rejected as `WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_INVALID`; parse the raw body before invoking payload-dependent verifiers.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
