          "body": "<!-- cubic:v=3f97a02f-f80e-4e02-a1d2-1297bd33dab6 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=54ce5ac6-5bcc-44ab-9d81-4a1baa574925 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: When an action accepts a `plugfnCustomCacheKey` parameter, custom and normal caching share the same entry and can return a result for the wrong request. Encode custom-key mode in a dedicated cache-key namespace or `generateKey` argument instead of representing it as ordinary params.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At plugfn/core/src/core/action-executor.ts, line 132:\n\n<comment>When an action accepts a `plugfnCustomCacheKey` parameter, custom and normal caching share the same entry and can return a result for the wrong request. Encode custom-key mode in a dedicated cache-key namespace or `generateKey` argument instead of representing it as ordinary params.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -126,7 +126,13 @@ export class ActionExecutor {\n+          ? this.cacheMiddleware.generateKey(\n+              provider,\n+              action,\n+              { plugfnCustomCacheKey: options.cache.key },\n+              options.userId,\n+              connection.id\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLg",
      "path": "plugfn/core/src/core/workflow-engine.ts",
      "line": 487,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615110",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Re-throw workflow trigger failures**\n\nWhen an enabled workflow step throws, this handler logs the failure and resolves successfully. `WebhookHandler.emit()` therefore treats the workflow handler as successful, records the event as processed, and the HTTP route marks its delivery successful and returns 200, so neither the provider nor the durable delivery worker retries the failed workflow. Re-throw after logging so the webhook remains retryable.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLj",
      "path": "plugfn/python/plugfn/core/workflow_engine.py",
      "line": 114,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615113",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register enabled Python workflows with the webhook handler**\n\nWhen callers enable a persisted Python workflow, this only changes its database status; `WorkflowEngine` never uses its injected `webhook_handler` to register the workflow's trigger. Consequently, incoming provider webhooks cannot invoke any workflow enabled through the public `workflows.enable()` API. Enabling, disabling, and deleting workflows need to maintain the corresponding trigger binding.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLm",
      "path": "plugfn/providers/src/gmail/index.ts",
      "line": 394,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615116",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Consume every page of Gmail incremental history**\n\nWhen Gmail returns more history records than `maxResults`, `users.history.list` includes a continuation token, but this response type omits it and the implementation processes only this first page before returning the response's current `historyId`. `runGmailSync()` then persists that ID as the new checkpoint, so all message additions on subsequent pages are permanently skipped. Follow `nextPageToken` until exhausted before advancing the checkpoint.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLo",
      "path": "plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts",
      "line": 524,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615119",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reclaim webhook deliveries abandoned in running state**\n\nIf a delivery worker exits after `claimWebhookDeliveriesForRetry()` changes a row to `running` but before the handler updates it, this query can never select that row again because it considers only `pending` and `failed` statuses. The claim metadata and `updatedAt` are not used as a lease cutoff, so a single worker crash permanently strands the delivery; include stale `running` claims in the retry candidates.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLq",
      "path": "plugfn/core/src/core/plug-fn.ts",
      "line": 343,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615122",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose readiness for workflow trigger rehydration**\n\nWhen a process starts with enabled workflows already in durable storage, trigger registration runs in an unawaited background task and `plugFn()` returns immediately. A webhook received while the storage query is pending has no workflow handler, is acknowledged successfully, and is permanently lost; a transient top-level rehydration failure is likewise only logged with no retry. Initialization should not expose the webhook router until rehydration has completed successfully.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZLr",
      "path": "plugfn/providers/src/stripe/index.ts",
      "line": 140,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:36:14Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788615123",
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include metadata when creating payment intents**\n\nWhen `paymentIntents.create` receives its declared `metadata` parameter, the form body is built only from amount, currency, customer, and description. The action succeeds but Stripe receives none of the caller's metadata; append the entries using Stripe fields such as `metadata[key]`, as is already done for customer creation.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ZeZaK",
      "path": "plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts",
      "line": 1034,
      "comments": [
        {
          "createdAt": "2026-08-15T05:37:11Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3788616423",
          "author": "pullfrog",
          "body": "The failed delivery remains scheduled even if a same-key provider re-delivery creates a sibling delivery that succeeds. `claimWebhookDeliveriesForRetry` selects failed rows without checking sibling success, so when this time arrives the logical webhook can be dispatched again after it already completed.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Prevent sibling delivery retries after receipt success\n\n## Affected sites\n- `plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts:1030-1035` — schedules the original failed delivery.\n- `plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts:1041-1068` — permits a same-key provider re-delivery while no sibling has succeeded yet.\n- `plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts:517-585` — later claims the original failed row using only its status and due time.\n- `plugfn/core/src/core/plug-fn.ts:731-750` — executes every claimed delivery without checking for a successful sibling.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep retry ownership mutually exclusive per receipt so a successful delivery makes all sibling failed deliveries non-runnable.\n- Cover failure, same-key provider re-delivery success, then due-delivery processing and assert that the handler is not invoked again.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Reuse one delivery record for direct retries, or make claim eligibility exclude receipts that already have a successful delivery.\n````\n\n</details>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
"}

