      "html_url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/103#discussion_r3810280001",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unknown sinks before advancing sync checkpoints**\n\nWhen a caller supplies a misspelled or unregistered `sinkId` for a provider sync definition, this lookup returns undefined and the later branch merely counts every item as skipped. The job is then marked completed and its checkpoint is persisted, so those records may never be offered to the corrected sink; fail with `SYNC_SINK_NOT_FOUND`, as the fallback-action path already does, instead of silently advancing.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
