      "body": "Pub/Sub may redeliver one message with a different top-level `deliveryAttempt`, so this stable `messageId` can map to a different raw payload hash. The existing hash-conflict branch then returns `409` instead of acknowledging the retry as a duplicate; compare immutable message content or exclude delivery metadata.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Keep Gmail Pub/Sub redeliveries deduplicable\n\n## Affected sites\n- `plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts:889` — hashes the entire wrapped push envelope.\n- `plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts:934-943` — rejects a stable key when any envelope byte changes.\n- `plugfn/core/src/router/http-router.ts:1272` — now uses Pub/Sub `messageId` as that stable key.\n- `plugfn/core/tests/e2e/webhook-verification.test.ts:570-607` — retries identical bytes and cannot detect delivery-attempt changes.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Redeliveries of one Pub/Sub message must return the duplicate acknowledgement even when delivery-specific envelope metadata changes, while distinct messages remain isolated.\n- Cover the same `messageId` with a changed `deliveryAttempt`.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Compare a canonical logical Pub/Sub message or omit delivery-specific fields from the Gmail payload hash.\n- Google documents wrapped push envelopes and `deliveryAttempt`: https://cloud.google.com/pubsub/docs/push\n- Gmail documents that this field is the Cloud Pub/Sub message ID: https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/guides/push\n````\n\n</details>"
